[36m(main_task pid=2959448)[0m Doc 3(Title: "Montreal Protocol") Montreal Protocol The Montreal Protocol on Substances that Deplete the Ozone Layer (a protocol to the Vienna Convention for the Protection of the Ozone Layer) is an international treaty designed to protect the ozone layer by phasing out the production of numerous substances that are responsible for ozone depletion. It was agreed on 26 August 1987, and entered into force on 26 August 1989, followed by a first meeting in Helsinki, May 1989. Since then, it has undergone eight revisions, in 1990 (London), 1991 (Nairobi), 1992 (Montreal), 1997 (Vienna), 1998 (Bogotá), 2007 (Montreal), 2009 (Vilnius) and 20016... (Kigali). As of September 2017, the only significant change in policy brought about by an amendment to the Protocol occurred in 2007, when it was decided that developed countries would bear the burden of providing financial support to developing countries for the increased costs of phasing out HCFC refrigerants in order to comply with the Protocol. These funds are provided through three mechanisms: the Multilateral Fund for the Implementation of the Montreal Protocol (MLF), the Clean Development Mechanism (CDM) established under the Kyoto Protocol, and Joint Implementation (JI) between developed nations</information><think>
